   "difficulty": "medium",
   "text": "In a permutation $a _ { 1 }... a _ { n }$, of n distinct integers, an inversion is a pair $( a _ { i }, a _ { j } )$ such that $i < j$ and $a _ { i } > a _ { j }$ If all permutations are equally likely, what is the expected number of inversions in a randomly chosen permutation of $1 \\ldots n?$",
   "options": [
    "$\\frac { n ( n - 1 ) } { 2 }$",
    "$\\frac { n ( n - 1 ) } { 4 }$",
    "$\\frac { n ( n + 1 ) } { 4 }$",
    "$2 n [ \\log _ { 2 } n ]$"
   ],
   "answer": [
    1
