   "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-3-21-17",
   "topic": "sql",
   "kind": "pyq",
   "type": "mcq",
   "marks": 2,
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "text": "Consider the set of relations shown below and the SQL query that follows. Students: (Roll\\_number, Name, Date\\_of\\_birth) Courses: (Course\\_number, Course\\_name, Instructor) Grades: (Roll\\_number, Course\\_number, Grade) Which of the following sets is computed by the above query?",
   "options": [
    "Names of students who have got an A grade in all courses taught by Korth",
    "Names of students who have got an A grade in all courses",
    "Names of students who have got an A grade in at least one of the courses taught by Korth",
    "None of the above"
   ],
   "answer": [
    2
   ],
   "code_blocks": [
    {
     "lang": "txt",
     "code": "Select distinct Name\nfrom Students, Courses, Grades\nwhere Students.Roll_number=Grades.Roll_number\nand Courses.Instructor = 'Korth'\nand Courses.Course_number = Grades.Course_number\nand Grades.Grade = 'A'"
    }
   ],
   "origin": {
    "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
    "volume": "filter1_volume3",
    "ref": "3.21.17",
    "exam": "GATE CSE 2003 | Question: 86",
    "section": "SQL",
    "paper_question": "86",
    "tags": [],
    "topic_source": "section"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-3-21-18",
   "topic": "sql",
   "kind": "pyq",
   "type": "mcq",
   "marks": 2,
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "text": "The employee information in a company is stored in the relation Employee (name, sex, salary, deptName) Consider the following SQL query It returns the names of the department in which",
   "options": [
    "the average salary is more than the average salary in the company",
    "the average salary of male employees is more than the average salary of all male employees in the company",
    "the average salary of male employees is more than the average salary of employees in same the department",
    "the average salary of male employees is more than the average salary in the company"
   ],
   "answer": [
    3
   ],
   "code_blocks": [
    {
     "lang": "txt",
     "code": "Select deptName\n  From Employee\n  Where sex = 'M'\n  Group by deptName\n  Having avg(salary) >\n    (select avg (salary) from Employee)"
    }
   ],
   "origin": {
    "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
    "volume": "filter1_volume3",
    "ref": "3.21.18",
    "exam": "GATE CSE 2004 | Question: 53",
    "section": "SQL",
    "paper_question": "53",
    "tags": [],
    "topic_source": "section"
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-3-21-19",
   "topic": "sql",
   "kind": "pyq",
   "type": "mcq",
   "marks": 2,
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "year": 2016,
   "text": "The relation book (title, price) contains the titles and prices of diferent books. Assuming that no two books have the same price, what does the following SQL query list?",
   "options": [
    "Titles of the four most expensive books",
    "Title of the fifth most inexpensive book",
    "Title of the fifth most expensive book",
    "Titles of the five most expensive books"
   ],
   "answer": [
    3
   ],
   "code_blocks": [
    {
     "lang": "sql",
     "code": "select title\nfrom book as B\nwhere (select count(*)\n  from book as T\n  where T.price>B.price) < 5"
    }
   ],
   "origin": {
    "source_file": "filter1_volume3.pdf",
    "volume": "filter1_volume3",
    "ref": "3.21.19",
    "exam": "GATE CSE 2005 | Question: 77, ISRO2016-55",
    "section": "SQL",
