  {
   "id": "mineru-filter1-volume3-3-21-38",
   "topic": "sql",
   "kind": "pyq",
   "type": "nat",
   "marks": 2,
   "difficulty": "medium",
   "text": "Consider a database that has the relation schema EMP (EmpId, EmpName, and DeptName). An instance of the schema EMP and a SQL query on it are given below: | EMP\n| EmpId | EmpName | DeptName\n| 1 | XYA | AA\n| 2 | XYB | AA\n| 3 | XYC | AA\n| 4 | XYD | AA\n| 5 | XYE | AB\n| 6 | XYF | AB\n| 7 | XYG | AB\n| 8 | XYH | AC\n| 9 | XYI | AC\n| 10 | XYJ | AC\n| 11 | XYK | AD\n| 12 | XYL | AD\n| 13 | XYM | AE The output of executing the SQL query is",
   "options": [],
   "answer_value": 2.6,
   "tolerance": 0.01,
   "code_blocks": [
    {
     "lang": "sql",
     "code": "SELECT AVG(EC.Num)\nFROM EC\nWHERE (DeptName, Num) IN\n    (SELECT DeptName, COUNT(EmpId) AS\n        EC(DeptName, Num)\nFROM EMP\nGROUP BY DeptName)"
    }
   ],
